Usage: copilot plugin marketplace add <source>

Add a marketplace.

Registers a new marketplace source so its plugins can be discovered and
installed.

Arguments:
  <source>
          Marketplace source (owner/repo for GitHub, URL, or local
          path)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  # Add a marketplace from a GitHub repository
  $ copilot plugin marketplace add github/copilot-plugins

  # Add a marketplace from a URL
  $ copilot plugin marketplace add https://example.com/marketplace.git
  $ copilot plugin marketplace add ssh://git@example.com/marketplace.git

Learn More:
  Use `copilot <command> --help` for more information about a command.
  Read the documentation at https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli
